{
  "rationale": "The plant automata G1 models the robot's perception of obstacles and motion capabilities, separating sensing (uncontrollable) and actuation (controllable) in a single automaton. The specification automata E1-E4 bind perception outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions, enforce conservative but non-oscillatory recovery, and ensure full_rotate is only used as a last resort. The design maximizes coverage by prioritizing forward/random_walk in clear states, uses short directed turns for obstacle recovery, and only uses move_backward and full_rotate in dedicated, justified states.",
